1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,100
This is so good!

2
00:00:14,760 --> 00:00:15,680
Real good?

3
00:00:15,840 --> 00:00:20,500
The worst thing about the dungeon is not being able to eat this good when we're in it.

4
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:22,540
Let's savor it while we can.

5
00:00:23,980 --> 00:00:25,420
Hey there, Kabru!

6
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:28,100
Haven't seen you around.

7
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:30,580
I heard you've been doing amazing lately.

8
00:00:31,060 --> 00:00:33,180
Well, I don't know about amazing.

9
00:00:33,720 --> 00:00:36,460
Seems like yesterday you all were just a bunch of rookies.

10
00:00:36,780 --> 00:00:37,740
But look at you now.

11
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:40,540
It's great you guys are still together.

12
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:43,580
Big parties are rare these days.

13
00:00:44,060 --> 00:00:45,420
Why do you think that is?

14
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:48,420
They go missing or just get sick of each other.

15
00:00:48,920 --> 00:00:50,760
Fighting over money is a big reason.

16
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:56,160
But your party's been together for a while, so maybe you'll be the ones to kill the Mad Mage.

17
00:00:56,160 --> 00:00:57,920
Yeah, right.

18
00:00:58,380 --> 00:01:00,000
We're not that good yet.

19
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,320
Don't sell yourself short.

20
00:01:05,420 --> 00:01:06,760
Why are you like that?

21
00:01:07,240 --> 00:01:07,520
Huh?

22
00:01:08,160 --> 00:01:12,360
Instead of playing coy with that idiot, you should have just come right out and said it.

23
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:15,460
Of course we'll be the ones to take out the Mad Mage.

24
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:19,540
We could never settle for being bottom-rung adventurers such as that, Goon.

25
00:01:19,540 --> 00:01:27,880
Wren, Wren, they'll know us all by our actions instead of our words.

26
00:01:29,960 --> 00:01:30,880
Here's the plan.

27
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:32,960
Today we'll go deeper into the dungeon.

28
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:35,200
Let's gear up and get ready.

29
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:46,340
Welcome.

30
00:01:47,340 --> 00:01:48,040
Hello there.

31
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:50,940
One week's food and two days' water for six people, please.

32
00:01:52,280 --> 00:01:53,240
Here you go.

33
00:01:53,240 --> 00:02:01,120
Dealing with food is a bigger pain than the monsters the deeper down we go.

34
00:02:01,540 --> 00:02:03,280
A week's worth of food is heavy.

35
00:02:04,060 --> 00:02:05,660
Some people stay in for a month.

36
00:02:05,860 --> 00:02:06,800
How do they do it?

37
00:02:07,520 --> 00:02:08,240
Well, McBell...

38
00:02:09,180 --> 00:02:12,240
What they do is...

39
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:18,240
They kill the parties they meet and feast on their flesh!

40
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:25,780
It'd be way easier to hunt monsters for food than other parties.

41
00:02:26,340 --> 00:02:28,600
You are what folks call a wet blanket.

42
00:02:36,740 --> 00:02:41,820
For our first time going down this deep, we're doing amazing.

43
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:44,480
At this rate, we're going to get farther than anyone.

44
00:02:45,320 --> 00:02:47,760
Well, we're doing great so far, but stay sharp.

45
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:50,060
Who knows what's waiting up ahead?

46
00:02:50,980 --> 00:02:53,380
I heard things have been strange here lately.

47
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:56,660
Some say the monsters are getting more aggressive.

48
00:02:57,340 --> 00:02:59,360
Others say the layout here has been changing.

49
00:03:00,020 --> 00:03:02,440
It definitely feels a lot weirder than before.

50
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:04,940
Better to be safe than sorry.

51
00:03:05,220 --> 00:03:05,620
Kaurburu!

52
00:03:06,420 --> 00:03:07,300
Look at this!

53
00:03:07,640 --> 00:03:08,840
I got it off this zombie!

54
00:03:09,620 --> 00:03:10,400
Let's open it.

55
00:03:10,900 --> 00:03:12,880
Don't waste your time with that thing.

56
00:03:13,580 --> 00:03:14,700
What's the harm in checking?

57
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:16,220
There could be gold in it.

58
00:03:16,220 --> 00:03:19,460
We've never found anything good in those before.

59
00:03:20,180 --> 00:03:24,700
There must be a good reason why this zombie had a death grip on it, literally speaking.

60
00:03:25,500 --> 00:03:27,360
It would be dumb to not take a peek.

61
00:03:28,260 --> 00:03:28,560
Huh?

62
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:30,100
No way!

63
00:03:30,820 --> 00:03:31,880
Gold and jewels!

64
00:03:32,380 --> 00:03:33,580
We hit the jackpot!

65
00:03:33,580 --> 00:03:36,480
We're rich!

66
00:03:36,740 --> 00:03:37,960
I can't believe it!

67
00:03:38,040 --> 00:03:38,600
Hot diggity.

68
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:39,580
What a hole.

69
00:03:41,820 --> 00:03:45,300
I thought by now the dungeon would be picked clean of all the treasure.

70
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:46,700
Oh well.

71
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:49,180
Like they say, things happen strange here.

72
00:03:49,180 --> 00:03:57,160
We so needed a brick like this.

73
00:03:57,640 --> 00:04:00,120
Now we can afford the supplies we need to go deeper.

74
00:04:01,600 --> 00:04:04,440
Guys, how about we all head back to town for some dinner?

75
00:04:04,940 --> 00:04:05,620
Does that sound good?

76
00:04:05,620 --> 00:04:06,580
Yeah!

77
00:04:06,580 --> 00:04:06,860
Yeah!

78
00:04:13,860 --> 00:04:14,380
Huh?

79
00:04:15,220 --> 00:04:15,740
Whoa.

80
00:04:16,580 --> 00:04:18,760
These guys got wiped out big time.

81
00:04:18,940 --> 00:04:19,520
Oh no.

82
00:04:19,840 --> 00:04:22,000
Looks like they were headed back to town too.

83
00:04:22,540 --> 00:04:23,400
How awful.

84
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:25,860
I don't see any wounds on them.

85
00:04:26,360 --> 00:04:27,480
Maybe a ghost killed them.

86
00:04:28,340 --> 00:04:29,960
Or they starved to death.

87
00:04:30,420 --> 00:04:33,340
And it looks to me like they killed each other over this treasure.

88
00:04:33,340 --> 00:04:38,860
I, um, I'm sure the corpse retrievers will find them soon.

89
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:41,820
But I'll cast a spell so they don't turn into zombies.

90
00:04:42,600 --> 00:04:44,620
This was Fallon's specialty though.

91
00:04:49,500 --> 00:04:51,580
What do you want to do about all this treasure?

92
00:04:52,260 --> 00:04:54,120
Let's pile it up and leave it for them.

93
00:04:54,660 --> 00:04:58,140
I bet most of it's gonna end up in the pockets of the corpse retrievers.

94
00:05:00,460 --> 00:05:00,860
What?

95
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:02,320
Are you okay back there?

96
00:05:02,560 --> 00:05:02,900
Yeah.

97
00:05:03,340 --> 00:05:03,860
Sure am.

98
00:05:05,140 --> 00:05:06,600
Why'd my sword twitch?

99
00:05:09,380 --> 00:05:11,100
Hey, let go of my hand.

100
00:05:11,680 --> 00:05:13,040
You're gonna give yourself away.

101
00:05:13,340 --> 00:05:14,160
What do you want?

102
00:05:16,960 --> 00:05:17,520
Hurry.

103
00:05:18,060 --> 00:05:18,880
Draw me.

104
00:05:19,480 --> 00:05:21,800
I can feel it telling me there's danger.

105
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:22,140
Marcel!

106
00:05:27,620 --> 00:05:28,020
Ah!

107
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:33,000
Marcel!

108
00:05:33,360 --> 00:05:34,240
Get away from there!

109
00:05:34,460 --> 00:05:34,620
Ah!

110
00:05:34,620 --> 00:05:35,620
Huh?

111
00:05:39,620 --> 00:05:40,620
Huh?

112
00:05:59,620 --> 00:06:01,620
A stun spell.

113
00:06:01,620 --> 00:06:05,620
I'm glad it wasn't an explosion spell.

114
00:06:05,620 --> 00:06:08,620
What the heck? Treasure insects?

115
00:06:08,620 --> 00:06:09,620
Oh, gross!

116
00:06:11,620 --> 00:06:15,620
Bees killed them? Never seen one up close like this before.

117
00:06:15,620 --> 00:06:18,620
I can't tell the difference from real treasure.

118
00:06:18,620 --> 00:06:20,620
But a minute ago you could tell.

119
00:06:20,620 --> 00:06:23,620
Yeah, he's right. You even drew your sword.

120
00:06:23,620 --> 00:06:27,620
Oh, um, I thought I saw one of them move?

121
00:06:27,620 --> 00:06:28,620
Liar.

122
00:06:28,620 --> 00:06:31,620
The critter and my sword sensed them.

123
00:06:31,620 --> 00:06:34,620
It's calm now, so that's gotta be it.

124
00:06:36,620 --> 00:06:39,620
Is it just me or is it getting weirder?

125
00:06:39,620 --> 00:06:40,620
Huh?

126
00:06:40,620 --> 00:06:41,620
Hmm.

127
00:06:41,620 --> 00:06:42,620
Yum.

128
00:06:42,620 --> 00:06:45,620
You have got to be kidding me.

129
00:06:45,620 --> 00:06:46,620
You have got to be kidding me.

130
00:06:46,620 --> 00:07:00,620
These you can eat. These you can't.

131
00:07:00,620 --> 00:07:02,620
Do they taste any good?

132
00:07:02,620 --> 00:07:04,620
Oh, I'll say they do.

133
00:07:04,620 --> 00:07:06,620
Bugs got all the nutrients a body needs.

134
00:07:06,620 --> 00:07:09,620
Cook these suckers up right and you got yourself a meal.

135
00:07:09,620 --> 00:07:12,620
Hell, they're a feast for the eyes, too.

136
00:07:12,620 --> 00:07:14,620
Not if you're seeing it from this angle.

137
00:07:14,620 --> 00:07:17,620
How can you tell which are or aren't edible?

138
00:07:17,620 --> 00:07:19,620
Hmm, it depends.

139
00:07:19,620 --> 00:07:21,620
For example, this one's easy.

140
00:07:21,620 --> 00:07:26,620
If you look between the beads, you can see its teeny legs.

141
00:07:26,620 --> 00:07:29,620
With brooches and coins, you check the backside.

142
00:07:29,620 --> 00:07:33,620
I think it's neat how the male and female coin bugs have different faces.

143
00:07:33,620 --> 00:07:36,620
With rings, if they're flexible, they're a bug.

144
00:07:36,620 --> 00:07:40,620
Tiaras need to be put in water to tell for sure.

145
00:07:40,620 --> 00:07:45,620
Bugs are light, so if it floats, you got yourself bugs.

146
00:07:45,620 --> 00:07:49,620
Let's cook these suckers before the stun spell wears off.

147
00:07:49,620 --> 00:07:52,620
For the necklace, pull off all the legs.

148
00:07:52,620 --> 00:07:55,620
The texture ain't great if you leave them on.

149
00:07:55,620 --> 00:07:57,620
Then skewer and roast it.

150
00:07:57,620 --> 00:08:02,620
Heat up some oil and give the coin bugs a good frown, stomach side down.

151
00:08:02,620 --> 00:08:07,620
Drop in a pinch of salt and stir them so the oil gets around evenly.

152
00:08:07,620 --> 00:08:09,620
There.

153
00:08:09,620 --> 00:08:12,620
Flip them spine side up so they look pretty.

154
00:08:12,620 --> 00:08:16,620
Pour the tiara, pop out the eggs and larva from their nest.

155
00:08:16,620 --> 00:08:19,620
Risk it up in the pot and boil everything together.

156
00:08:21,620 --> 00:08:24,620
Spoon it into a jar and...

157
00:08:24,620 --> 00:08:26,620
It's ready.

158
00:08:26,620 --> 00:08:33,620
Looks nice, but they still don't look much like food to me.

159
00:08:33,620 --> 00:08:37,620
Then again, it's not my first time eating these things.

160
00:08:37,620 --> 00:08:39,620
I heard they're some kind of regional cuisine.

161
00:08:39,620 --> 00:08:41,620
Some say eating them brings luck.

162
00:08:41,620 --> 00:08:43,620
I'll find out in a sec.

163
00:08:45,620 --> 00:08:48,620
Those taste way better than the ones I had.

164
00:08:48,620 --> 00:08:50,620
Of course it does.

165
00:08:50,620 --> 00:08:54,620
The monsters you get from the dungeon always got better flavor than the ones on the surface.

166
00:08:54,620 --> 00:08:59,620
Folks up top can try raising them, but they just don't taste the same.

167
00:08:59,620 --> 00:09:00,620
Uh...

168
00:09:00,620 --> 00:09:01,620
Uh...

169
00:09:01,620 --> 00:09:02,620
Uh...

170
00:09:02,620 --> 00:09:03,620
Uh...

171
00:09:03,620 --> 00:09:04,620
Uh...

172
00:09:04,620 --> 00:09:05,620
Uh...

173
00:09:05,620 --> 00:09:06,620
Uh...

174
00:09:06,620 --> 00:09:07,620
Uh...

175
00:09:07,620 --> 00:09:08,620
Uh...

176
00:09:08,620 --> 00:09:09,620
Uh...

177
00:09:09,620 --> 00:09:11,620
Dear lord, it's creamy.

178
00:09:11,620 --> 00:09:14,620
I'm never gonna wear neckses again.

179
00:09:14,620 --> 00:09:16,620
This kinda tastes like fish.

180
00:09:16,620 --> 00:09:17,620
Ow!

181
00:09:17,620 --> 00:09:20,620
If we find some deeper down, they'll taste even better.

182
00:09:20,620 --> 00:09:21,620
I can't wait.

183
00:09:21,620 --> 00:09:22,620
Oh!

184
00:09:22,620 --> 00:09:23,620
Thank you.

185
00:09:23,620 --> 00:09:24,620
Ow!

186
00:09:24,620 --> 00:09:25,620
Mm.

187
00:09:25,620 --> 00:09:26,620
Mm.

188
00:09:26,620 --> 00:09:27,620
Mm.

189
00:09:27,620 --> 00:09:28,620
Wow.

190
00:09:28,620 --> 00:09:29,620
That's sweet.

191
00:09:29,620 --> 00:09:32,620
Can't get over how real they look.

192
00:09:32,620 --> 00:09:35,620
They use mimicry to hide from their enemies.

193
00:09:35,620 --> 00:09:37,620
Just like you, sword critter.

194
00:09:37,620 --> 00:09:40,620
Is that why you reacted to them?

195
00:09:40,620 --> 00:09:41,620
Hmm.

196
00:09:41,620 --> 00:09:42,620
Mm.

197
00:09:42,620 --> 00:09:43,620
Mm.

198
00:09:43,620 --> 00:09:44,620
Can I try one?

199
00:09:44,620 --> 00:09:45,620
Hm.

200
00:09:45,620 --> 00:09:46,620
Hmm.

201
00:09:46,620 --> 00:09:47,620
Hmm.

202
00:09:47,620 --> 00:09:48,620
Hmm.

203
00:09:48,620 --> 00:09:49,620
Huh?

204
00:09:49,620 --> 00:09:50,620
Huh?

205
00:09:50,620 --> 00:09:51,620
Huh?

206
00:09:51,620 --> 00:09:52,620
It's nothing.

207
00:09:52,620 --> 00:09:53,620
Oh.

208
00:09:53,620 --> 00:09:54,620
It thought it was a threat.

209
00:09:54,620 --> 00:09:55,620
It was trying to warn me.

210
00:09:55,620 --> 00:09:56,620
I think it thinks we're a team now.

211
00:09:56,620 --> 00:09:57,620
How cute.

212
00:09:57,620 --> 00:09:58,620
I have to give you a name.

213
00:09:58,620 --> 00:09:59,620
Ready to get going?

214
00:09:59,620 --> 00:10:02,620
What are we supposed to do with the ones you said we can't eat?

215
00:10:02,620 --> 00:10:03,620
Toss them, if you want.

216
00:10:03,620 --> 00:10:04,620
If someone were to eat one of these, what would you do?

217
00:10:04,620 --> 00:10:05,620
What would you do?

218
00:10:05,620 --> 00:10:06,620
What would you do with the ones you said we can't eat?

219
00:10:06,620 --> 00:10:08,620
Toss them, if you want.

220
00:10:08,620 --> 00:10:09,620
If someone were to eat one of these, what would you do?

221
00:10:09,620 --> 00:10:10,620
What would you do with them?

222
00:10:10,620 --> 00:10:12,620
Are they poisonous or do they just taste bad?

223
00:10:12,620 --> 00:10:13,620
What are you talking about?

224
00:10:13,620 --> 00:10:14,620
You'd break your teeth.

225
00:10:14,620 --> 00:10:15,620
You can't eat real treasure.

226
00:10:15,620 --> 00:10:16,620
You could break your teeth.

227
00:10:16,620 --> 00:10:17,620
You can't eat real treasure.

228
00:10:17,620 --> 00:10:18,620
What would you do with me?

229
00:10:18,620 --> 00:10:19,620
What would you do with them now?

230
00:10:19,620 --> 00:10:20,620
How cute.

231
00:10:20,620 --> 00:10:21,620
I have to give you a name?

232
00:10:21,620 --> 00:10:22,620
Ready to get going?

233
00:10:22,620 --> 00:10:23,620
What are we supposed to do with the ones you said we can't eat?

234
00:10:23,620 --> 00:10:24,620
Toss them, if you want.

235
00:10:24,620 --> 00:10:25,620
If someone were to eat one of these, what would happen to them?

236
00:10:25,620 --> 00:10:26,620
Don't you tell them, not to their own house?

237
00:10:26,620 --> 00:10:27,620
You need to drink.

238
00:10:27,620 --> 00:10:28,620
What are you talking about?

239
00:10:28,620 --> 00:10:30,620
You break your teeth.

240
00:10:30,620 --> 00:10:35,620
You can't eat real treasure.

241
00:10:35,620 --> 00:10:38,620
You break your teeth.

242
00:10:38,620 --> 00:10:40,740
Real treasure. Real treasure.

243
00:10:41,620 --> 00:10:43,200
Treasure. Treasure.

244
00:10:43,860 --> 00:10:46,320
Why didn't you say that before?

245
00:10:49,740 --> 00:10:50,620
Got it.

246
00:10:50,840 --> 00:10:52,640
From now on, your name's Kensuke.

247
00:11:05,120 --> 00:11:07,360
You're eating another one of those things?

248
00:11:07,360 --> 00:11:08,880
We got a lot of leftovers.

249
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:11,580
Honestly, this isn't a picnic.

250
00:11:17,720 --> 00:11:19,540
Great. The temperature dropped.

251
00:11:21,140 --> 00:11:23,420
All those shimmery blobs.

252
00:11:24,640 --> 00:11:26,380
Yeah, those are ghosts gathering.

253
00:11:26,980 --> 00:11:28,680
Go, before they see us.

254
00:11:30,040 --> 00:11:30,720
Ghosts?

255
00:11:31,200 --> 00:11:33,660
They're drawn to the corpses we just left behind.

256
00:11:33,660 --> 00:11:37,660
Hmm. We should just blast them with a spell and...

257
00:11:38,460 --> 00:11:40,620
That's right.

258
00:11:41,260 --> 00:11:42,340
Fallon's not here.

259
00:11:43,240 --> 00:11:44,140
I miss her, too.

260
00:11:45,180 --> 00:11:47,480
I cast a protection spell on that party.

261
00:11:48,140 --> 00:11:50,660
I had to rush it a bit, but the ghosts won't possess...

262
00:11:51,360 --> 00:11:58,620
Ghost. Behind us. Run!

263
00:11:58,620 --> 00:12:17,140
Oh, that idiot!

264
00:12:17,140 --> 00:12:27,940
My ears.

265
00:12:27,940 --> 00:12:29,800
Hurry, get up. More are coming.

266
00:12:32,800 --> 00:12:34,980
They're all riled up from that explosion.

267
00:12:34,980 --> 00:12:40,680
Don't you know any less flashy magic spells?

268
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:42,540
You know, something simple?

269
00:12:42,700 --> 00:12:44,300
Like the kind Fallon always used.

270
00:12:44,580 --> 00:12:45,680
Are you kidding me?

271
00:12:45,820 --> 00:12:47,280
She used high-level magic.

272
00:12:47,480 --> 00:12:49,220
There was nothing simple about it.

273
00:12:49,300 --> 00:12:49,600
Really?

274
00:12:49,940 --> 00:12:50,480
Oh, yeah.

275
00:12:51,060 --> 00:12:51,720
It's true.

276
00:12:52,360 --> 00:12:53,800
She's an awesome magic user.

277
00:12:54,720 --> 00:12:56,920
Dealing with ghosts was no sweat for her.

278
00:12:56,920 --> 00:12:58,580
Lifgant.

279
00:12:59,460 --> 00:13:00,100
Odenbaum.

280
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:02,560
There!

281
00:13:03,160 --> 00:13:04,440
That's all there is to it.

282
00:13:05,040 --> 00:13:07,060
Those pesky ghosts can't harm you now.

283
00:13:08,720 --> 00:13:12,760
If any show up, an explosion spell could take them all out quick.

284
00:13:13,280 --> 00:13:14,680
You could do that easy, Fallon.

285
00:13:17,300 --> 00:13:20,300
If possible, I'd prefer to avoid doing that.

286
00:13:21,040 --> 00:13:22,380
It doesn't get rid of them.

287
00:13:22,820 --> 00:13:25,640
After they're blown to bits, they just reform again anyway.

288
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:27,800
And I don't want to make them suffer.

289
00:13:28,480 --> 00:13:29,800
You're so kind.

290
00:13:29,980 --> 00:13:32,320
That's nice you're giving them the benefit of the doubt.

291
00:13:33,880 --> 00:13:36,380
But if ghosts go around possessing people's bodies...

292
00:13:37,120 --> 00:13:40,740
I think they deserve to get their butts kicked.

293
00:13:46,600 --> 00:13:47,240
Mm-hmm.

294
00:13:47,780 --> 00:13:50,340
That guy's on the missing adventurer list, all right.

295
00:13:50,340 --> 00:13:53,680
Okay, I'll take care of them.

296
00:13:54,240 --> 00:13:55,820
First, I'll knock them...

297
00:13:55,820 --> 00:13:57,620
I'll do it.

298
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:00,140
This can be handled without violence.

299
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:02,320
No!

300
00:14:02,680 --> 00:14:03,420
Fallon, wait!

301
00:14:15,420 --> 00:14:16,540
Be at peace.

302
00:14:17,240 --> 00:14:18,300
And leave this body.

303
00:14:20,340 --> 00:14:25,040
Fallon!

304
00:14:31,840 --> 00:14:33,860
She sounds like a heck of a person.

305
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:35,040
Yeah.

306
00:14:35,480 --> 00:14:36,780
Fallon was amazing.

307
00:14:37,100 --> 00:14:37,900
I mean, is.

308
00:14:38,880 --> 00:14:39,720
But...

309
00:14:39,720 --> 00:14:42,340
If the ghosts catch up to us...

310
00:14:42,340 --> 00:14:45,260
I'll have to use my magic to stop them.

311
00:14:45,260 --> 00:14:46,580
Oh, no, you won't.

312
00:14:46,800 --> 00:14:49,340
There's no way you can blow up every single one of them.

313
00:14:53,400 --> 00:14:55,380
I'll do it just like Fallon did.

314
00:14:56,040 --> 00:14:58,440
I'll give them all a gentle embrace.

315
00:14:58,900 --> 00:15:00,940
A gentle embrace of explosions.

316
00:15:01,180 --> 00:15:01,440
No.

317
00:15:01,600 --> 00:15:02,080
Gentle explosions.

318
00:15:02,080 --> 00:15:02,240
No!

319
00:15:02,720 --> 00:15:03,100
No!

320
00:15:03,500 --> 00:15:06,780
You said yourself you can't do it like Fallon, so just leave them alone!

321
00:15:06,920 --> 00:15:08,600
She'd trust me to do the right thing!

322
00:15:09,060 --> 00:15:11,240
Okay, then what will you do if you run out of mana?

323
00:15:11,440 --> 00:15:12,120
I won't.

324
00:15:12,220 --> 00:15:15,060
I can use my weaker explosion spells to blow them up.

325
00:15:15,260 --> 00:15:17,300
There are no weak explosion spells!

326
00:15:17,460 --> 00:15:18,520
Guys, enough.

327
00:15:18,940 --> 00:15:22,320
Hate to say it, folks, but it don't look like we're gonna outrun these creepies.

328
00:15:23,420 --> 00:15:27,740
The longer we stand around arguing, the faster they'll catch up to us.

329
00:15:29,060 --> 00:15:31,080
Wait, what are you doing?

330
00:15:31,480 --> 00:15:34,180
Gonna whip up a little something to keep the ghosts off us.

331
00:15:34,980 --> 00:15:36,140
What kind of thing?

332
00:15:36,340 --> 00:15:37,540
A holy water thing.

333
00:15:37,740 --> 00:15:38,960
Wait, you have holy water?

334
00:15:39,500 --> 00:15:39,760
Nope.

335
00:15:40,280 --> 00:15:41,080
Gotta make some.

336
00:15:41,780 --> 00:15:43,340
You can make that?

337
00:15:43,720 --> 00:15:45,260
Didn't know you were a cleric, too.

338
00:15:47,180 --> 00:15:50,360
There's all kinds of custom in the world to get rid of evil stuff.

339
00:15:51,700 --> 00:15:52,720
Fire's one of them.

340
00:15:53,200 --> 00:15:55,980
It keeps the dark back, and it can create and destroy.

341
00:15:56,560 --> 00:16:02,500
All through history, folks have used it as a sacred symbol and a holy ward to keep that evil the hell away from you.

342
00:16:02,500 --> 00:16:07,020
Yeah, I know all that, but candles aren't gonna keep ghosts back.

343
00:16:07,340 --> 00:16:11,360
One candle might not help much, but a bunch of them all lit up and flickering away?

344
00:16:11,780 --> 00:16:13,060
That's a lot of holy power.

345
00:16:13,700 --> 00:16:16,320
The golden rhinoceros beetle's another secret thing.

346
00:16:16,720 --> 00:16:20,020
To some folks, they were symbols of the sun and the sun god.

347
00:16:20,600 --> 00:16:22,160
A lot of love for those critters.

348
00:16:23,260 --> 00:16:24,360
Ooze is holy, too.

349
00:16:24,360 --> 00:16:28,820
It's used as an offering to the gods and to purify whatever it is it needs purifying.

350
00:16:30,380 --> 00:16:31,420
Then there's salt.

351
00:16:31,780 --> 00:16:36,000
Tradition's going way back, saying it protects against evil and purifies the body.

352
00:16:36,760 --> 00:16:39,180
And since sugar looks the same, I'll add some of that.

353
00:16:39,620 --> 00:16:42,820
Not sure how potent it'll be, so I'll dump a bunch in to be safe.

354
00:16:43,060 --> 00:16:44,520
You're making this up as you go!

355
00:16:45,200 --> 00:16:46,840
Not a bad idea to add some herbs.

356
00:16:47,200 --> 00:16:49,400
And what the heck, dried monster guts, too.

357
00:16:49,400 --> 00:16:52,160
Then we'll add the power of fire to the mix.

358
00:16:55,200 --> 00:16:56,860
The holy water's ready.

359
00:17:01,080 --> 00:17:02,060
Here they come!

360
00:17:02,480 --> 00:17:05,100
Just gotta make sure the lid's tight on the holy water.

361
00:17:05,500 --> 00:17:07,500
What are you doing? Aren't you gonna use it?

362
00:17:07,620 --> 00:17:10,320
I will, as soon as I tie this rope to the jar.

363
00:17:13,140 --> 00:17:14,820
We're gonna die here.

364
00:17:19,400 --> 00:17:24,600
Oh, no.

365
00:17:26,740 --> 00:17:27,300
Thelen.

366
00:17:31,640 --> 00:17:32,820
I'm alive.

367
00:17:33,540 --> 00:17:34,320
Because of you.

368
00:17:35,680 --> 00:17:38,280
If only the dragon ate me instead,

369
00:17:39,200 --> 00:17:41,040
our friends wouldn't be in this mess.

370
00:17:43,640 --> 00:17:44,560
Forgive me.

371
00:17:44,560 --> 00:18:09,040
Holy crap!

372
00:18:09,340 --> 00:18:10,980
I saw my dad on the other side!

373
00:18:12,980 --> 00:18:14,220
It's working.

374
00:18:14,880 --> 00:18:17,380
Every ghost he hits gets driven away.

375
00:18:23,140 --> 00:18:24,480
Only water works.

376
00:18:24,800 --> 00:18:25,720
Even in a jar.

377
00:18:25,940 --> 00:18:27,180
It works amazingly.

378
00:18:30,460 --> 00:18:34,080
Maybe I've been possessed this whole time by Fallon.

379
00:18:34,620 --> 00:18:36,140
How could you say that?

380
00:18:36,380 --> 00:18:37,340
Fallon would never.

381
00:18:37,740 --> 00:18:39,880
And she hasn't even turned into a ghost yet.

382
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:41,460
No, that's not what I mean.

383
00:18:41,460 --> 00:18:45,440
I couldn't get over the fact that we don't have her help.

384
00:18:45,820 --> 00:18:48,340
And thinking about how easy things would be if we did.

385
00:18:48,980 --> 00:18:51,060
But the reality is, she's not here.

386
00:18:52,340 --> 00:18:54,720
Until she's back, we gotta help ourselves.

387
00:18:54,720 --> 00:18:59,760
Yeah, you're right.

388
00:19:01,380 --> 00:19:01,880
Senchi!

389
00:19:01,880 --> 00:19:04,300
Let me take a crack at him.

390
00:19:04,300 --> 00:19:12,960
It's over.

391
00:19:12,960 --> 00:19:21,960
It's over.

392
00:19:21,960 --> 00:19:26,800
The jar's got frost on it.

393
00:19:28,200 --> 00:19:31,860
Using holy water like that's more efficient than spraying it all over.

394
00:19:32,340 --> 00:19:33,160
That figures.

395
00:19:33,580 --> 00:19:36,020
Ghost can pass through the jar so the water hits him.

396
00:19:36,500 --> 00:19:36,740
Hmm?

397
00:19:37,800 --> 00:19:39,120
Well, I'll be.

398
00:19:39,120 --> 00:19:46,400
It's sorbet.

399
00:19:51,900 --> 00:19:55,340
Is it safe to eat something with ghost funk all over it?

400
00:19:55,820 --> 00:20:00,560
I'm more worried about what holy water this powerful is gonna do to our stomachs.

401
00:20:00,780 --> 00:20:03,280
I'm worried about how much sugar I've had today.

402
00:20:03,280 --> 00:20:09,480
It's great!

403
00:20:16,280 --> 00:20:17,200
He's right!

404
00:20:17,540 --> 00:20:18,140
It's good!

405
00:20:18,500 --> 00:20:20,480
It's so light and refreshing, too!

406
00:20:22,420 --> 00:20:25,100
Instead of getting cursed by ghosts, we got blessed.

407
00:20:25,500 --> 00:20:26,340
You said it!

408
00:20:26,340 --> 00:20:28,420
You said there's monster in this.

409
00:20:28,640 --> 00:20:29,500
What did you end up using?

410
00:20:30,100 --> 00:20:31,600
Just some grated slime guts.

411
00:20:32,300 --> 00:20:34,420
Oh, that explains the jiggly texture.

412
00:20:34,780 --> 00:20:36,840
But it's still so smooth and creamy.

413
00:20:39,840 --> 00:20:40,880
Hey, guys.

414
00:20:41,780 --> 00:20:42,880
Get this.

415
00:20:44,180 --> 00:20:45,560
We're so lucky.

416
00:20:45,920 --> 00:20:48,840
If Fallon didn't get eaten, we wouldn't be having sorbet now.

417
00:20:50,480 --> 00:20:51,120
Huh?

418
00:20:52,120 --> 00:20:53,600
You're joking, right?

419
00:20:53,600 --> 00:20:56,680
It sounds like you're happy that she got eaten.

420
00:20:56,800 --> 00:20:59,080
You're, like, the worst brother ever!

421
00:20:59,380 --> 00:21:02,000
But I was just saying...

422
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:04,920
You know, some things are better to keep to yourself.

423
00:21:06,740 --> 00:21:11,300
Oh, jeez.

424
00:21:11,560 --> 00:21:12,940
If only Fallon were here.

425
00:21:14,340 --> 00:21:17,140
There's a positive side to every bad situation.

426
00:21:17,620 --> 00:21:20,100
She'd say something like that and pack me up.

427
00:21:21,040 --> 00:21:23,780
I don't know if it's me or this sorbet,

428
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:25,800
but the vibe here got chillier.

429
00:21:26,500 --> 00:21:27,820
Come back, Fallon.

430
00:21:27,960 --> 00:21:28,960
We need you!

